      "writtenOn": "2021-04-19T12:20:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Got it. I just send this patch to android12-5.10 for review.\n\nAs for android 11, some customer using i.MX device are still under development. From below log \u003cwithout this patch\u003e, we can see that the interrupt of timer@306a0000 mainly exists on one cpu, which means more power consumption； while \u003cwith this patch\u003e, its interrupt spread on each cpu.\n\n\u003cWithout this patch\u003e\nevk_8mp:/ # cat /proc/interrupts  | grep timer\n  3:      10611      10462      12703      10320     GICv3  30 Level     arch_timer\n 26:         54          0          0       9402     GICv3  79 Level     timer@306a0000\n\n\u003cWith this patch\u003e\nevk_8mp:/ # cat /proc/interrupts | grep timer\n  3:       9431       7959      10607       8023     GICv3  30 Level     arch_timer\n 26:        466        914        838       1097     GICv3  79 Level     timer@306a0000",
      "parentUuid": "b3e2988b_5ffa452e",
